Notes:
For venv version after 3.13, the .venv automatically generated the .gitignore file inside so you do not have to worry about excluding those environment packages manually when using git.  

## Basics
# Create python environment through following command
python3 -m venv <env name>.venv

#execute the environment
source <env name>/bin/activate

# find out installed packages 
pip list

# Exit the environment 
typing deactivate in cmd


## Create projects with vscode
- source the env
- go to the folder of your project and turn on vscode code.
